WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.260
Accelerate an electron through a voltage,

2
00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:04.710
and it picks up kinetic energy.

3
00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:08.010
Every moving electron
also has a wavelength.

4
00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:11.910
Push it through a bigger voltage,
and that wavelength shrinks.

5
00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:14.560
An electron microscope relies on this.

6
00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:17.950
It needs a wavelength
below the size of an atom.

7
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.220
Now aim far smaller: a wavelength
shorter than a single proton.

8
00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:26.140
How much energy would one electron need?

9
00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:30.580
In this mission, you'll link an electron's
wavelength to the voltage that accelerates

10
00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:31.240
it.

11
00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:35.140
Then you'll compare an electron and a
proton with the same kinetic energy,

12
00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:37.960
and see whose wavelength is longer.

13
00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:42.570
Your mission: estimate the energy an
electron needs for a wavelength smaller than

14
00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:43.390
a proton.
